"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[109],{60109:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"schemaVersion":1,"locale":"en","slug":"04-nadezhnaya-chast","title":"Lesson 04. Portfolio Defensive Armor: Deposits, OFZs, and Money Market Instruments","sourceFingerprint":"19b309c64dc221ea2fae9187e506d5e03cd34f587ae8f3d78ccf23e40eb6724c","blocks":[{"id":"b001","markdown":"# Chapter 4. Portfolio Protective Armor: Deposits, OFZ, and Money Market Instruments"},{"id":"b002","markdown":"*MakeCash Book \xb7 Volume II: Capital Protection: 20 Years Against Inflation*  \\n*Thoughtful reading time: ~7 minutes*"},{"id":"b003","markdown":"> \\"The strength of a foundation is determined not by its external luster, but by its ability to withstand earthquakes. The protective portion of savings must be strictly conservative: its goal is not to break yield records, but to guarantee that you preserve capital during any market storm.\\""},{"id":"b004","markdown":"An investment portfolio must certainly include a sector of absolute tranquility. It is free from speculative surges of tens of percent, as well as sudden price collapses. The primary purpose of this money is to reliably safeguard what has been accumulated, slightly outpace real consumer price inflation, and build a financial buffer while aggressive instruments weather market turbulence."},{"id":"b005","markdown":"The protective perimeter absorbs emergency safety funds (cushions), savings allocated for specific expenses on a 12 to 36-month horizon, and that baseline share of long-term investments whose temporary drawdown is psychologically unacceptable to you. In the domestic market, this framework is traditionally built from three key elements: **term deposits**, **government bonds (OFZ)**, and **exchange-traded liquidity funds**."},{"id":"b006","markdown":"## Macroeconomic Landscape: The Interest Rate Cycle"},{"id":"b007","markdown":"When making decisions on conservative instruments, one must be guided by monetary benchmarks:"},{"id":"b008","markdown":"* At the meeting on October 23, 2026, the regulator kept the key rate at **14%**.\\n* Yields on classic deposits in the top 10 credit institutions stabilized by the end of October at **13.06%** (in the second ten-day period) and **13.09%** (in the third ten-day period).\\n* The macroeconomic consensus forecast for 2027 predicts a decrease in the average key rate to **12.8%**, while the Central Bank\'s own baseline benchmark is in the **10.5–12.5%** range (with a forecast range of 12.5–13.5% in the autumn release)."},{"id":"b009","markdown":"```\\n   High Rate Cycle                     Monetary Easing Period\\n   ═════════════════════►              ════════════════════►\\n   Key rate: 14%                       Forecast: 10.5–12.5%\\n   (Time to lock in yields)            (Yields on new deposits drop)\\n```"},{"id":"b010","markdown":"> **Investor Rule:** When the economy approaches the phase of decreasing cost of money, it is strategically advantageous to lock in the maximum interest rate for the longest available term in advance."},{"id":"b011","markdown":"## Instrument 1: Classic Bank Deposit"},{"id":"b012","markdown":"A bank deposit remains the most straightforward and accessible solution for an individual. The contract is executed in a matter of minutes, the interest rate is documented and fixed, and the risks are protected by the state."},{"id":"b013","markdown":"* **State Guarantees.** The deposit insurance system via the DIA provides a full refund of up to **1.4 million ₽** per depositor within a single bank (including accrued interest). Savings exceeding this limit require distribution across different independent credit institutions.\\n* **Yield Lock-in.** The main advantage of a non-callable deposit during a monetary policy reversal is a guaranteed rate. If the bank signed an agreement with you at 13% per annum for 12 months, then even with a sharp drop in market rates to 11%, your payouts will not decrease by a single kopeck."},{"id":"b014","markdown":"**Pitfalls and Limitations:**\\n1. *Loss of income upon early termination:* it is impossible to urgently withdraw funds without forfeiting almost all accrued interest.\\n2. *Marketing conditions:* top-tier rates often apply exclusively to \\"new funds\\" or require the purchase of paid subscriptions or insurance policies.\\n3. *Taxation:* cumulative income across all accounts exceeding the tax-exempt threshold is subject to personal income tax under standard rules."},{"id":"b015","markdown":"## \uD83E\uDDEE Calculation in the Notebook Margins"},{"id":"b016","markdown":"### Example: The Effect of Locking in Rates During CBR Policy Easing"},{"id":"b017","markdown":"Imagine you have **450 000 ₽**, and 30 days after opening the account, the regulator lowers the yield benchmark to 11% per annum."},{"id":"b018","markdown":"| Calculation Parameter | 1-Year Deposit (13% rate) | Savings Account (floating rate) |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Deposit amount** | 450 000 ₽ | 450 000 ₽ |\\n| **Yield in Month 1** | 13.0% per annum | 13.0% per annum |\\n| **Yield for Months 2 to 12** | 13.0% (locked in) | 11.0% (declined following the market) |\\n| **Total result for the year** | **58 500 ₽** | **50 250 ₽** |\\n| **Net difference in your pocket** | **+8 250 ₽ in favor of the fixed-rate deposit** | — |"},{"id":"b019","markdown":"*The calculation is based on simple interest without compounding, using average market indicators (13.09%).*"},{"id":"b020","markdown":"## Term Synchronization: Aligning Assets with Life Plans"},{"id":"b021","markdown":"The main mistake of beginners is opening a single deposit \\"for everything at once\\". It is much more practical to split the amount into target pools across time horizons:"},{"id":"b022","markdown":"* **Vacation trip in 4 months (budget: 120 000 ₽).**  \\n  *Where to direct:* a short four-month deposit or a high-yield savings account with daily balance calculation.\\n* **Major bathroom renovation in 9 months (budget: 180 000 ₽).**  \\n  *Where to direct:* a targeted non-callable deposit for exactly 9 months fixing a high rate.\\n* **Tuition for a child\'s first university year in 2 years (budget: 150 000 ₽).**  \\n  *Where to direct:* a two-year deposit at current peak rates or OFZ maturing in 24 months."},{"id":"b023","markdown":"With this approach, you will not have to prematurely close long-term products and forfeit accrued interest, while an emergency fund is more sensibly kept in a savings account or on the exchange-traded money market, where withdrawals are available instantly."},{"id":"b024","markdown":"## Tool 2: Federal Loan Bonds (OFZ)"},{"id":"b025","markdown":"By purchasing OFZ, you are lending to the Ministry of Finance of the Russian Federation. The state guarantees regular coupon payments and is obligated to repay the nominal value of the bond (typically **1 000 ₽**) on the maturity date. Bonds are purchased through a broker or via an Individual Investment Account (IIS-3)."},{"id":"b026","markdown":"### Key differences from a standard deposit:\\n* **Unlimited safety volume:** there is no 1.4 million ₽ limit here, as the sovereign financial system acts as the guarantor.\\n* **Liquidity without loss of earned income:** you can sell the bond on MOEX on any business day. You retain the accrued coupon income (ACI), though the bond\'s exchange price at that moment can be either higher or lower than your purchase price.\\n* **Long horizon:** unlike banks, which rarely open deposits for longer than 3 years, OFZ allow you to \\"lock in\\" attractive yields for 10–15 years."},{"id":"b027","markdown":"### Government Bond Lineup"},{"id":"b028","markdown":"| Issue category | Coupon payment mechanism | Optimal use case |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **OFZ-PD (fixed income)** | Coupon size is fixed for the entire circulation period of the bond | An easing cycle by the CBR is expected; the goal is to lock in yield for years ahead |\\n| **OFZ-PK (variable coupon / floaters)** | Payment is tied to the money market rate (RUONIA) | Market uncertainty, protection against a prolonged period of high money costs |\\n| **OFZ-IN (inflation-indexed principal)** | Principal is indexed daily to the inflation rate + coupon | Concerns over an uncontrolled inflation shock |"},{"id":"b029","markdown":"### OFZ Yield Map along the MOEX Curve\\n* 1-year issue: **14,36%**\\n* 3-year issue: **15,76%**\\n* 5-year issue: **16,25%**\\n* 10-year issue: **16,52%**"},{"id":"b030","markdown":"```\\n▲ Yield to maturity (%)\\n│                                              ● 10 years: 16,52%\\n│                                ● 5 years: 16,25%\\n│                  ● 3 years: 15,76%\\n│    ● 1 year: 14,36%\\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────► Maturity (years)\\n```"},{"id":"b031","markdown":"> **Remember the interest rate risk:** The further away the bond\'s maturity date, the more volatile its market price. If rates in the country rise, older issues with lower coupons drop in price. However, if you hold the bond strictly until maturity, market fluctuations do not matter: the state will return the nominal 1 000 ₽ and pay all promised coupons."},{"id":"b032","markdown":"## Tool 3: Exchange-Traded Money Market Funds"},{"id":"b033","markdown":"Money market funds (for example, those focused on REPO transactions with the Central Counterparty) invest capital in ultra-short secured loans backed by high-grade securities. The unit price of such a fund increases smoothly each business day at a pace comparable to the CBR key rate."},{"id":"b034","markdown":"According to MOEX data, by the fall of 2026, net assets of such funds crossed the **2 trillion ₽** threshold, and the aggregate investor base exceeded **3 million people** (asset growth over three quarters amounted to **+31%**)."},{"id":"b035","markdown":"```\\n   ┌───────────────────────┐   Loans backed by collateral    ┌─────────────────────────┐\\n   │   Money market fund   │ ◄─────────────────────────────► │   Central Counterparty  │\\n   │  (share grows every   │  (daily return at key rate)     │      (MOEX clearing)    │\\n   │     business day)     │                                 │                         │\\n   └───────────────────────┘                                 └─────────────────────────┘\\n```"},{"id":"b036","markdown":"**Pros of the instrument:**\\n* Maximum flexibility: entry threshold starts from just a few rubles per share.\\n* No \\"freeze\\": the asset can be sold on any trading day without forfeiting accrued gains.\\n* Available within an IIS with eligibility for state tax benefits."},{"id":"b037","markdown":"**Specifics and cons:**\\n* No DIA insurance protection (though infrastructure risk is minimized).\\n* Floating yield: as soon as the CBR lowers the key rate, the fund share\'s growth rate synchronously slows down.\\n* Costs: the management company charges a management fee (usually within 1% per annum).\\n* Standard tax on profits upon withdrawal (unless the assets are sheltered by long-term holding tax relief or an IIS deduction)."},{"id":"b038","markdown":"## Summary Matrix of Conservative Assets"},{"id":"b039","markdown":"| Criterion | Bank Deposit | OFZ Bonds | Money Market Fund |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Entry point** | Mobile banking / branch | Brokerage account / IIS | Brokerage account / IIS |\\n| **Repayment guarantee** | DIA system (up to 1.4 million ₽) | Russian Federation | Secured by REPO transactions |\\n| **Yield type** | Fixed by contract | Fixed (for OFZ-PD) | Floating (tracks the rate) |\\n| **Access to principal** | Forfeiting interest | Instantly at market price | Instantly without loss of profit |\\n| **Main function** | Specific goals with a clear horizon | Securing yield for years ahead | Emergency fund, waiting for trades |"},{"id":"b040","markdown":"## \uD83D\uDCCB Practical Audit Algorithm"},{"id":"b041","markdown":"1. **Conduct an inventory of your accounts.** Write down all active deposits in a workbook: financial institution, balance, interest rate, and maturity date. Make sure that the amount with accrued interest does not exceed **1.4 million ₽** in any single institution.\\n2. **Align dates with your goals.** Check whether the deposit maturity date corresponds to the planned date of a major purchase. If the funds become available well before the event, plan a reinvestment instrument in advance.\\n3. **Optimize your emergency reserve.** Move your financial safety net away from non-interest-bearing card accounts. Transfer it to a liquidity fund or a savings account with interest accrued on the actual daily balance."}],"terms":[{"id":"ofz-pd","term":"OFZ-PD","definition":"federal loan bonds with a fixed coupon, locking in the interest rate until maturity."},{"id":"dohodnost-k-pogasheniyu","term":"Yield to Maturity (YTM)","definition":"the total annualized return on a bond if held until its maturity date."},{"id":"rusfar","term":"RUSFAR","definition":"the fair benchmark rate for secured money on the Moscow Exchange based on REPO transactions."},{"id":"asv","term":"DIA","definition":"the Deposit Insurance Agency, guaranteeing the reimbursement of bank deposits up to 1.4 million ₽."}],"quizzes":[{"id":"q1","q":"An investor expects the regulator to consistently cut the key rate over the next 2–3 years. Which strategy allows locking in the current record yield level for the longest horizon?","options":["Placing all available capital into a money market fund","Transferring funds to a savings account with daily capitalization","Purchasing long-term fixed-coupon OFZ-PD issues or opening a long-term deposit"],"correct":2,"explanation":"**Correct answer: C.** Money market funds and savings accounts will immediately lower their yield following the regulator\'s key rate cuts. Only a classic deposit and fixed-coupon OFZ issues guarantee locking in the stated rate for the entire term until maturity."},{"id":"q2","q":"What will happen to the market price of a previously purchased long-term bond with a 10% fixed coupon if the Central Bank suddenly hikes the key rate from 11% to 16%?","options":["The bond\'s market price will increase to compensate for market growth","The bond\'s market price will drop below par value, as higher-yielding instruments appear on the market","The market price will remain unchanged; only the nominal value will change"],"correct":1,"explanation":"**Correct answer: B.** The fundamental rule of interest rate risk applies: as monetary conditions tighten, the prices of previously issued low-coupon bonds fall on the exchange so that their yield to maturity matches new market realities."},{"id":"q3","q":"For which financial objectives is it most rational to use exchange-traded money market funds?","options":["For guaranteed receipt of coupon income 15 years ahead without rate risk","For holding emergency reserve funds and parking idle cash before buying target assets","For receiving state insurance coverage via the DIA up to 1.4 million ₽"],"correct":1,"explanation":"**Correct answer: B.** Liquidity funds are optimal for capital that might be needed at any moment: income is accrued daily, fund units can be sold without forfeiting accumulated yield, and price volatility is minimal. They are not covered by DIA deposit insurance."}],"officialSources":[]}')}}]);